    <statement><p>Suppose <m>y = \sin(-4 x^2 - 3 x-1)</m>.
We can write <m>y = \sin(u)</m>, where <m>u =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/> .
The Leibnitz notation for the chain rule is
<m>\displaystyle \frac{dy}{dx} = \frac{dy}{du} \cdot \frac{du}{dx}</m>.
The factors are <m>\displaystyle \frac{dy}{du} =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/> (written as a function of <m>u</m> ) and
<m>\displaystyle \frac{du}{dx} =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> .
Now substitue in the function of <m>x</m> for <m>u</m> to get</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \frac{dy}{dx} =</m> <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0004"/> (written as a function of <m>x</m> ).</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4xx+\left(-3\right)x+\left(-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\cos\mathopen{}\left(u\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-8x+\left(-3\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\cos\mathopen{}\left(-4xx+\left(-3\right)x+\left(-1\right)\right)\mathopen{}\left(-8x+\left(-3\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
